# Cafe Pulse KDS — sway compositor config
#
# MOK-49 / MOK-50 (KDS Pi Deployment phase 8).
#
# This file is installed at ~/.config/sway/config by the curl-bash setup
# flow (/api/kds/setup/[setupCode]). Sway is launched as a systemd user
# service (~/.config/systemd/user/kds-kiosk.service) on boot, with linger
# enabled so no console login is required.
#
# Multi-output story: two Chromium instances launched with distinct
# --class= app-ids. Each app-id is assigned to a workspace which is pinned
# to a specific HDMI output. Sway routes each window to the correct TV
# without xrandr-style detection logic in the kiosk script.

### Outputs ###################################################################
# Enable both HDMI outputs unconditionally. If only one is connected, sway
# silently parks the second workspace in a hidden state — no error, no
# crash. Output names follow the wlroots convention on Pi OS Bookworm.
output HDMI-A-1 enable
output HDMI-A-2 enable

# Never blank or suspend. Kiosk displays are always-on.
output * dpms on

### Workspaces ################################################################
# Pin workspace 1 to HDMI-A-1 (TV 1, screen slot 1).
# Pin workspace 2 to HDMI-A-2 (TV 2, screen slot 2).
workspace 1 output HDMI-A-1
workspace 2 output HDMI-A-2

### Window routing ############################################################
# kds-kiosk.sh launches two Chromium instances with --class=kds-screen-{1,2}.
# Chromium under Wayland exposes --class as the wl_surface app_id, so sway's
# assign rules match and route each browser window to the right workspace.
assign [app_id="kds-screen-1"] workspace 1
assign [app_id="kds-screen-2"] workspace 2

# Always fullscreen the routed windows so the KDS render fills each TV
# without title bars, gaps, or sway's tiling layout intervening.
for_window [app_id="kds-screen-1"] fullscreen enable
for_window [app_id="kds-screen-2"] fullscreen enable

### Kiosk niceties ############################################################
# Hide window decorations entirely.
default_border none
default_floating_border none
gaps inner 0
gaps outer 0
# Sway requires a positive font size even when there are no decorations to
# render. Setting to 8 (was: 0, which sway rejects as 'Invalid font size').
font pango:monospace 8

# We don't run any X11 apps under sway — Chromium uses Ozone Wayland
# natively. Skip Xwayland entirely so sway doesn't error trying to load
# the (intentionally uninstalled) Xwayland binary.
xwayland disable

# Hide the cursor after 1s of inactivity. Replaces the v2 `unclutter` daemon.
seat * hide_cursor 1000

# Focus-follows-mouse off — no mouse in a kiosk; eliminates accidental focus
# changes if a tech happens to plug in a keyboard for debugging.
focus_follows_mouse no

### Autostart ################################################################
# The kiosk script launches Chromium instances and waits on their PIDs.
# Logs go to ~/kds-kiosk.log and the systemd journal (via the unit's
# StandardOutput).
exec /home/pi/kds-kiosk.sh

### Debug / break-glass ######################################################
# If you ever need to escape the kiosk to a terminal for debugging, plug in
# a USB keyboard and press Mod4+Return. There's no default Mod for sway out
# of the box on a fresh install, so this is the lone binding we add — and
# only because operator debugging is the realistic on-Pi escape hatch.
# Comment out for hardened production builds.
set $mod Mod4
bindsym $mod+Return exec foot
